speechtext:
Asbestos is known to be present in the 1910 Wing of the East Block on mechanical pipes and most of the plaster walls and ceilings. The 1910 Wing is presently in a state of disrepair because little is being expended for maintenance in view of the upcoming major renovations proposed for this area of the building.
During the spring of 1990, it was decided that containment work should be carried out to ensure asbestos in deteriorated plaster walls or mechanical pipes was properly sealed and encapsulated and did not contaminate the environment. This remedial work was completed during the week-end of March 31, 1990 to April 1, 1990 and generally included the following:
-repairs of minor cracks in plaster walls;
-encapsulation of exposed asbestos material on mechanical pipes;
-clean up of loose material, as necessary, and proper disposal of materials;
Routine Proceedings
-installation of plastic barricades to cover major cracks in deteriorated walls to ensure the material is properly sealed.
The scope of this work has been reviewed, on site, with the contractor prior to issuing the work order. The contractor was made fully aware of the nature of the work involving remedial work in an asbestos environment in order that he may have the required equipment and protective work wear available.
In November 1990, another contractor was hired to carry out similar remedial work. The contractor was informed of the circumstances under which the remedial work would have to be performed.
